<https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/id/nsv-registry/Approved%20NSVs-alpha/LLT/CDASHIG%20%20v2.2>
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/nsv-registry#Approved%20NSVs-alpha> ;
    nsv:Curator%20Remarks """Check with the CDASH team.\r
Okayed by CDASH team - approved for next version of CDASHIG.  \r
NSV bc it is for interventions.\r
2022-09-14 Removed: "assigned to the event" since this is for "interventions" which is inconsistent with the SDTM v2.0 definition.  To place Jira: SDTM team consider dictionary type (MedDRA, ATC, etc.) variables be used in all domains and consider the definition reflect this. Currently, the definition assumes MedDRA can only be used for events.\r
09-28-2022 Added "assigned" back in the definition to be consistent with the other MedDRA variables.""" ;
    nsv:Define-XML%20Datatype "text" ;
    nsv:Description "The lowest-level term assigned from MedDRA." ;
    nsv:External%20Dictionary "MedDRA " ;
    nsv:Label "Lowest Level Term" ;
    nsv:Limited%20to%20Class%28es%29 "Interventions" ;
    nsv:Notes "These are coding variables using MedDRA that can be used in Intervention Domains since the current SDTM use is for the Events Domains." ;
    nsv:Qualifying%20Variable%28s%29 "TRT" ;
    nsv:Requester%20Remarks "THE CDASH TEAM IS requesting that all CDASH NSV variables published in the CDASHIG be entered into the NSV registry. CDASH has many coding variable to be added. This is just an example. This is one of the MedDRA coding terms that CDASH needs to add for the Intervention Class. Currently, these variables are only allowed in the Events domain. Some companies code procedures to MedDRA.   Additionally, CDASH wants to add the coding variables for Anatomical Therapeutic Chemical (ATC) classification system for CM. This topic may require discussion with the SDTM for harmonization in SDTM 4.0. Perhaps SDTM should create a new class of variables called coding variables, that can be used as needed in all domains. " ;
    nsv:Role "Non-Standard Variable Qualifier" ;
    nsv:Simple%20Datatype "Char" ;
    nsv:Source%28s%29 "CDASHIG  v2.2" ;
    nsv:Status%20of%20the%20NSV%20Review "Approved" ;
    nsv:Status%20of%20the%20Source%20Document "Published" ;
    nsv:Variable%20Name "LLT" ;
    nsv:XML%20Datatype "string" ;
.

<https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/id/nsv-registry/Approved%20NSVs-alpha/LLTCD/CDASHIG%20%20v2.2>
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/nsv-registry#Approved%20NSVs-alpha> ;
    nsv:Curator%20Remarks """The SDTM v2.0 definition is "The lowest-level term\r
code assigned to the\r
event from MedDRA." We removed the "assigned to the event" because this is related to interventions.  In the future, if it is allowed in SDTM the definition will have to change.""" ;
    nsv:Define-XML%20Datatype "integer" ;
    nsv:Description "The lowest-level term code assigned from MedDRA." ;
    nsv:External%20Dictionary "MedDRA" ;
    nsv:Label "Lowest Level Term Code" ;
    nsv:Limited%20to%20Class%28es%29 "Interventions" ;
    nsv:Publication%20Date%20of%20the%20Source%20Document "2021-09-28" ;
    nsv:Qualifying%20Variable%28s%29 "LLT" ;
    nsv:Role "Non-Standard Variable Qualifier" ;
    nsv:Simple%20Datatype "Num" ;
    nsv:Source%28s%29 "CDASHIG  v2.2" ;
    nsv:Status%20of%20the%20NSV%20Review "Approved" ;
    nsv:Status%20of%20the%20Source%20Document "Published" ;
    nsv:Variable%20Name "LLTCD" ;
    nsv:XML%20Datatype "float" ;
.

