<https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/id/nsv-registry/Approved%20NSVs-alpha/MRKSTR/TAUG-Rare%20Diseases%20v1.0>
    a <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/def/nsv-registry#Approved%20NSVs-alpha> ;
    nsv:Curator%20Remarks "Expected for possible promotion in the next version update of the SDTMIG (expand variable to be able to use in the BS domain)." ;
    nsv:Define-XML%20Datatype "text" ;
    nsv:Description "The text string identifying the full set of markers/indicators used by the laboratory to operationally define the complete test based on the combination of CPTEST, CPSBMRKS, and CPCELSTA. Because laboratories often use different markers/indicators to identify a cell population, the relationship between a named cell population in CPTEST (as combined with CPSBMRKS and CPCELSTA values) and the set of markers used to identify that population is many-to-one. To ensure nuances important for accurately interpreting the data are accounted for and which arise from the use of different sets of markers, it is necessary to operationally define the test in terms of the complete set of markers/indicators used to perform that test." ;
    nsv:Label "Marker String" ;
    nsv:Requester%20Remarks "Per SDTM v2.0, the variable for Marker String (MRKSTR) is only permitted in the CP domain. Therefore, it is included in this BS dataset as non-standard variable." ;
    nsv:Role "Non-Standard Record Qualifier" ;
    nsv:Simple%20Datatype "Char" ;
    nsv:Source%28s%29 "TAUG-Rare Diseases v1.0" ;
    nsv:Status%20of%20the%20NSV%20Review "Approved" ;
    nsv:Status%20of%20the%20Source%20Document "Review for Publication" ;
    nsv:Used%20in%20Domain%28s%29 "BS (Biospecimen Findings)" ;
    nsv:Used%20in%20WIKI%20Example%28s%29 "159336529" ;
    nsv:Variable%20Name "MRKSTR" ;
    nsv:XML%20Datatype "string" ;
.

